# 21: Web - Vue.js + Tailwind CSS

**Authority Type:** Frontend Framework Stack  
**Technology:** Vue 3 + Composition API + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS  
**Module ID:** `frontend/vue-tailwind`

---

## Purpose

Enforce Vue.js 3 Composition API patterns, TypeScript integration, and Tailwind CSS standards for component development.

---

## Core Principles

### 1. Composition API over Options API
Use `<script setup>` with Composition API for all new components.

**Rationale:** Better TypeScript support, better code organization, better reusability.

### 2. TypeScript for Type Safety
All components, composables, and utilities MUST be TypeScript.

### 3. Tailwind for Styling
Use Tailwind utility classes, avoid custom CSS except for animations and complex layouts.

### 4. Single File Components (SFC)
Standard `.vue` structure: `<script setup>`, `<template>`, `<style scoped>`.

---

## Component Standards

### Component Structure

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref, computed, onMounted } from 'vue';
import type { User } from '@/types';

interface Props {
  userId: string;
  initialData?: User;
}

const props = defineProps<Props>();

const emit = defineEmits<{
  save: [user: User];
  cancel: [];
}>();

// Reactive state
const user = ref<User | null>(props.initialData ?? null);
const loading = ref(false);

// Computed properties
const displayName = computed(() => 
  user.value ? `${user.value.firstName} ${user.value.lastName}` : ''
);

// Methods
async function loadUser() {
  loading.value = true;
  try {
    // Load user data
  } finally {
    loading.value = false;
  }
}

// Lifecycle
onMounted(() => {
  if (!props.initialData) {
    loadUser();
  }
});
</script>

<template>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
    <div v-if="loading" class="flex items-center justify-center">
      <span class="text-gray-500">Loading...</span>
    </div>
    
    <div v-else-if="user" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
        {{ displayName }}
      </h2>
      
      <button
        @click="emit('save', user)"
        class="rounded-md bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
        data-testid="user-save-button"
      >
        Save Changes
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<style scoped>
/* Only for animations or complex layouts not possible with Tailwind */
.fade-enter-active,
.fade-leave-active {
  transition: opacity 0.3s;
}

.fade-enter-from,
.fade-leave-to {
  opacity: 0;
}
</style>
```

### Naming Conventions

**Components:**
- PascalCase: `UserProfile.vue`, `DataTable.vue`
- Multi-word names: `UserProfileCard.vue` (not `User.vue`)

**Props:**
- camelCase in script: `userId`, `initialData`
- kebab-case in template: `<UserProfile :user-id="id" />`

**Events:**
- camelCase: `emit('updateUser', user)`
- kebab-case in template: `@update-user="handleUpdate"`

**Composables:**
- Prefix with `use`: `useUser.ts`, `useAuth.ts`, `useForm.ts`

